' A real, ordinary ArcoBASIC program meant to be compiled BY the Fission
' Compiler Substrate's native x86-64 backend (fission/amir/lower_x86_64.abas)
' -- see fission/tests/native_programs/hello_native.abas's own header
' comment for the directory convention. This one exercises Phase 3's own
' construct set: real user-declared FUNCTIONs, a genuine SysV-shaped
' calling convention (arguments in %rdi/%rsi/..., return value in %rax,
' independent stack frames per call), and real recursion -- each call gets
' its own frame on the actual hardware call stack.
'
' Recursive Fibonacci, 0 through 12, plus one direct check that a
' multi-parameter call and a deeper recursive call both still land on the
' right stack frame. Expected output verified against legacy
' `ArcoFission compile-run` on this identical source as the equivalence-
' testing oracle.
FUNCTION Fib(n)
    IF n <= 1 THEN
        RETURN n
    END IF
    RETURN Fib(n - 1) + Fib(n - 2)
END FUNCTION

FUNCTION Sum(a, b)
    RETURN a + b
END FUNCTION

FOR i = 0 TO 12
    PRINT Fib(i)
NEXT
PRINT Sum(Fib(10), Fib(11))
